  "title": "Preparing the Shroud (Kafan) of the Dead",
  "data": "When he has fulfilled his term by death, his eyes should be closed, his hands stretched out, his mouth shut, his legs straightened, his jaw bound, and his shroud prepared. The shroud is required to consist of three pieces: an apron, a shirt and a wrapper. It is recommended, however, to add a fourth piece, a special Yemeni wrap or any other wrapper; a fifth piece of cloth with which the thighs and hips are bound; and a sixth piece as a turban.\nIn addition, camphor that has not been touched by fire should be used, in a quantity of thirteen and a third dirhams, or four mithqals, or at least one dirham. If even this is not possible, any quantity may be used.\nOn each piece of the shroud, the following words may be written, with the dead person's name in place of “so-and-so”:\nفُلَانٌ يَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ وَاَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ وَاَنَّ عَلِيًّا اَمِيْرُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْاَئِمَّةَ مِنْ وُلْدِهٖ\nFULAANUN YASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAHOO WA ANNA MUHAMMADAN RASOOLULLAAHI WA ANNA A'LIYYAN AMEERUL MU'MINEENA WAL A'IMMATA MIN WULDIH\nSo-and-so bears witness that there is no god but Allah, One, having no partner, that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and that Ali is the Commander of the Faithful, and the Imams from his descendants...\nThen the names of the Imams may be written. This inscription may be written with water in which soil from the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.), or asba' (apparently the soil of a certain mountain), has been mixed. It must not be written in black."
}
